From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Derek Ross <derekross@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 11:35:13 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: max17042_battery: tell the MAX77759 model load
 timeouts apart

The MAX77759 model load waits twice after setting Config2.LdMdl: for
the gauge to clear LdMdl, and for RepCap, which the load procedure
zeroes first, to become non-zero again. Both timeouts print the same
"model load did not complete: -110".

On a Pixel 7 Pro (gs201) that message appears only on the first boot
after the battery ran flat (issue #169: at 3.26 V it failed, two hours
later at 3.87 V on the same kernel it loaded). The cheetah model's
VEmpty is 0xa561, an empty voltage of 3.30 V, so on such a cell the
model's RepCap is 0 and the second wait can time out even when the
load itself completed.

Keep the message for LdMdl and give the RepCap wait its own, with the
cell voltage, so that a log tells which of the two it was.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: Derek Ross <derekross@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/power/supply/max17042_battery.c | 23 ++++++++++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/max17042_battery.c b/drivers/power/supply/max17042_battery.c
index 725066381..c045436e5 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/max17042_battery.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/max17042_battery.c
@@ -1454,12 +1454,25 @@ static int max77759_fg_load_params(struct max17042_chip *chip)
 				       !(val & MAX77759_FG_CONFIG2_LDMDL),
 				       MAX77759_FG_LDMDL_POLL_US,
 				       MAX77759_FG_LDMDL_TIMEOUT_US);
-	if (!ret)
-		ret = regmap_read_poll_timeout(map, MAX17042_RepCap, val, val,
-					       MAX77759_FG_LDMDL_POLL_US,
-					       MAX77759_FG_LDMDL_TIMEOUT_US);
-	if (ret)
+	if (ret) {
 		dev_err(chip->dev, "model load did not complete: %d\n", ret);
+		return ret;
+	}
+
+	/*
+	 * RepCap was zeroed above and comes back once the gauge has run the
+	 * new model. A cell below VEmpty is empty by the model, so its RepCap
+	 * can stay 0 even after a good load.
+	 */
+	ret = regmap_read_poll_timeout(map, MAX17042_RepCap, val, val,
+				       MAX77759_FG_LDMDL_POLL_US,
+				       MAX77759_FG_LDMDL_TIMEOUT_US);
+	if (ret) {
+		if (regmap_read(map, MAX17042_VCELL, &val))
+			val = 0;
+		dev_err(chip->dev, "RepCap still 0 after the model load: %d (VCell %u mV)\n",
+			ret, val * MAX17042_VOLTAGE_LSB / 1000);
+	}
 
 	return ret;
 }
